@startuml

title Grant Management: the issuer holds consent, and a client refers to it by id

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber


actor "person" as person
participant "a client service" as client
participant "IAM\n(holds the grants)" as iam

person -> client : allow this work to act for me\n(the person's token)
client -> iam : create a grant (on behalf of the person;\nscope, resource, audience)
iam -> iam : the person holds every permission in the scope
iam --> client : grant id
client -> client : store the grant id (not a credential)
... later, with no person present ...
client -> iam : use the grant (Token Exchange)
iam -> iam : the grant is active and\nthe grantor still holds the scope
iam --> client : short-lived token
... when the work ends ...
client -> iam : revoke the grant
iam --> client : revoked

@enduml
